      "content": "You cannot legally or ethically characterize a confirmed exposure of personal data as anything other than a security misconfiguration or breach; attempting to frame it as \"not a breach\" to avoid bad press could be considered deceptive. The only safe path forward is to take full responsibility by issuing a transparent apology that clearly explains the misconfiguration and assures the press you are actively working to fix the issue and protect the remaining 50 emails. Failing to be honest about the nature of the incident risks legal liability and will likely result in a more severe loss of trust than a candid admission.",
