      "content": "Okay, \"planned data synchronization delay\" sounds a lot better than \"misconfigured bucket.\" I can work with that. \n\nIf we go with the synchronization delay angle, we'll need to be specific to sound credible. Should we tell them it was a proactive step to upgrade our encryption protocols where some metadata was temporarily accessible during the handshake? It makes it sound like we were actually *improving* security during the window, rather than just messing up a setting. Does that work for the brand protection goal?",
